---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../../data/site';

const updated = 'August 23, 2026';
const contact = site.contactEmail;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cuddle Crush — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Cuddle Crush, Squish ’Em, published by MonkeyPayPay."
>
  <article class="prose legal container">
    <a class="app__back" href="/#flagship">← Cuddle Crush</a>
    <h1>Cuddle Crush, Squish ’Em — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__meta">Published by MonkeyPayPay · Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>1. The short version</h2>
    <p>We collect what the game needs to work and almost nothing else.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You can play without giving us an email address.</li>
      <li>
        We do not use advertising SDKs, and no third-party analytics or tracking company receives
        your data.
      </li>
      <li>We never sell or rent your personal information.</li>
      <li>We never see your card details. Apple and Google handle payment.</li>
      <li>You can delete your account and everything attached to it from inside the game.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The rest of this document says the same things in the detail the law expects.</p>

    <h2>2. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      MonkeyPayPay (“we”, “us”) publishes the mobile game Cuddle Crush, Squish ’Em (“the Game”). We
      are the data controller for the information described here.
    </p>
    <p>Contact: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>

    <h2>3. What we collect, and why</h2>

    <h3>3.1 Your account</h3>
    <div class="legal__tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>What</th><th>Why we hold it</th><th>Required?</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>A profile identifier (a random ID)</td><td>Identifies your progress and your seat in a match</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Display name (up to 20 characters)</td><td>Shown to other players in matches, crews and leaderboards</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email address</td><td>Only if you register, so you can sign in on another device and recover your account</td><td>No — guest play needs none</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Password (stored only as a one-way hash)</td><td>Signing in. We cannot read your password</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Friend code</td><td>Lets other players add you deliberately rather than by searching</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Account creation date</td><td>Account security, and support requests</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Year of birth, if you enter it</td><td>Age-restricted features only (see §6). We ask for the year, never the full date</td><td>No</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      If you play as a guest we hold no email address and no password. That guest profile lives on our
      servers so your progress survives, but it is not linked to you personally by anything you have
      told us.
    </p>

    <h3>3.2 How you play</h3>
    <p>
      Match results, wins and losses, fighter levels, unlocked characters, seasonal rank, quest and
      battle-pass progress, and your balances of the three in-game currencies (Coins, Gems and
      Shards). This is the game’s save file. Without it there is no game.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also keep a record of every movement of in-game currency — what was earned or spent, when,
      and why. That record exists so that if you ever tell us your balance is wrong we can actually
      check, rather than guess.
    </p>

    <h3>3.3 Purchases</h3>
    <p>
      When you buy Gems or a subscription, Apple or Google processes the payment. We receive a
      purchase token, the product identifier, the amount of in-game currency granted, the price in US
      dollars from our own price table, and the time. We never receive your card number, billing
      address, or any other payment credential.
    </p>

    <h3>3.4 Things you write</h3>
    <p>
      Crew chat messages. The most recent 50 messages of a crew’s chat are stored so the conversation
      is there when you open it, and are filtered for profanity. Do not put anything private in chat:
      every member of the crew can read it.
    </p>
    <p>Player reports and blocks, so we can act on them.</p>

    <h3>3.5 Technical and diagnostic data</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Your IP address, used to rate-limit sign-in attempts and abusive traffic. It is not stored
        against your gameplay history as a profile field.
      </li>
      <li>Error reports the Game sends when something goes wrong, so we can fix it.</li>
      <li>
        Gameplay events — for example that a match ended, a box was opened, or a level was gained —
        recorded with your profile identifier and a timestamp. We use these to understand whether the
        game is balanced and where players get stuck.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These analytics are our own. They are written to our own server. They are not sent to an
      advertising network, a data broker, or a third-party analytics provider.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What we do NOT do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        No advertising SDKs. The Game contains no advertising network code. It has a “rewarded” bonus
        feature, and where that involves an ad partner in future this policy will be updated before
        that ships.
      </li>
      <li>No third-party trackers or analytics services.</li>
      <li>No selling or renting of personal information, to anyone, ever.</li>
      <li>No cross-app or cross-site tracking. We do not follow you anywhere else.</li>
      <li>No access to your contacts, photos, microphone, or precise location.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Our legal bases (UK/EU users)</h2>
    <div class="legal__tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Basis</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Running your account and the Game</td><td>Performance of a contract with you</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Purchases and preventing payment fraud</td><td>Contract, and our legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keeping the Game secure and fair</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Understanding and improving the Game</td><td>Legitimate interests</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Anything you explicitly opt into</td><td>Consent, which you may withdraw</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>6. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The Game is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 where local law sets that threshold),
      and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some features are age-restricted. Shardfall staking is limited by a self-declared year of birth
      and is unavailable to players under the required age. It uses Shards, an earned-only currency
      that cannot be bought and cannot be converted into money or anything of real-world value — it is
      not gambling.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you believe a child has given us personal information, contact us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Sharing</h2>
    <p>We share personal information only with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Apple and Google, to verify that a purchase is genuine and to learn when one has been refunded.</li>
      <li>
        Our hosting and database providers, who store the data on our behalf under contract and may
        not use it for their own purposes.
      </li>
      <li>Authorities, where the law actually requires it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Other players see your display name, your friend code if you give it to them, your fighters and
      your public record — wins, rank, and leaderboard position. They do not see your email address.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Where your data is held</h2>
    <p>
      Our servers and database are operated by our hosting provider and may be located outside your
      country. Where data leaves the UK or EEA we rely on the safeguards our providers offer,
      including standard contractual clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>9. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account data: while your account exists.</li>
      <li>After you delete your account: removed from our live systems immediately. Backups roll off within 30 days.</li>
      <li>
        Purchase and currency records: retained for up to 7 years where tax and accounting law
        requires it, even after account deletion. These are financial records; they are kept
        separately and are not used to rebuild a profile.
      </li>
      <li>Chat: only the most recent 50 messages per crew.</li>
      <li>Analytics events: retained for up to 24 months.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Wherever you live, you may ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>See what we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Correct anything that is wrong.</li>
      <li>
        Delete your account and its data. You can do this yourself: <strong>Account → Delete
        Account</strong>, inside the Game. It is immediate and it is not reversible.
      </li>
      <li>Export a copy of your data in a portable format.</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict how we use it.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent where we relied on it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. We will respond within 30 days and will not
      charge you or make the Game worse for asking.
    </p>
    <p>
      UK and EU users may complain to their data protection authority. In the UK that is the
      Information Commissioner’s Office (ico.org.uk).
    </p>
    <p>
      California residents: the rights above cover the CCPA/CPRA rights to know, delete, correct, and
      opt out of sale or sharing. We do not sell or share personal information as those terms are
      defined, so there is nothing to opt out of, and we will not discriminate against you for
      exercising any right.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Security</h2>
    <p>
      Passwords are stored only as one-way hashes and are never recoverable, by us or by anyone else.
      Sign-in attempts are rate-limited. Purchases are verified against Apple and Google and each
      purchase can be granted exactly once, so a replayed receipt cannot be used twice.
    </p>
    <p>
      No system is perfectly secure, and we will not pretend otherwise. If a breach affects you, we
      will tell you and the relevant regulator as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy materially — particularly if we ever add advertising or a third-party
      analytics service — we will say so in the Game before the change takes effect, not afterwards.
      The “last updated” date at the top always reflects the current version.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>MonkeyPayPay — <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>

    <hr />
    <p class="legal__note">
      Questions about this privacy policy? Contact <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. See
      also the <a href="/games/cuddle-crush/terms">Cuddle Crush Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal .todo {
    background: rgba(255, 176, 32, 0.16);
    color: #ffca6a;
    border: 1px dashed rgba(255, 176, 32, 0.5);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0 0.35em;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .legal h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
  }
  .legal__tablewrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .legal th,
  .legal td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .legal th {
    background: var(--surface);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
